ClipSync syncs text and image clipboards between trusted macOS and Linux
computers on your local network. It comes with a desktop app, a terminal UI
(`clipsync tui`) and a command-line tool. Computers connect to each other
directly over mutually authenticated TLS 1.3; there is no cloud service and no
account.

> **Experimental.** Text sync works between macOS and Arch Linux. Broader
> desktop coverage, sleep/wake and login/logout recovery are still being
> validated. Install the same release on every computer: older versions cannot
> pair by code.

